    "created_at": "2025-03-10T20:44:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-10T20:44:03Z",
    "body": "The problem is coming up with something that's more descriptive. \"Legacy\" makes some sense to me in that it's the legacy way of thinking about selections in terms of ranges. With composed ranges being the better way. If composed ranges were not there we'd prolly just call it \"range\", but I think that doesn't provide enough contrast with composed ranges and also doesn't dissuade API designers from building on top of it.",
